  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Pattukkottai?", answer: "Send us your child's programme, subject and level, and we match a tutor who has taught that syllabus recently. Lessons are live and online, so the tutor need not live in Pattukkottai. You get a short shortlist, a free trial lesson and a written rate before any paid session. Contact support@ibgram.com or WhatsApp +91 7439 368 115 with the subject, the exam session and a few convenient evening times." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Pattukkottai?", answer: "Yes, for Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel International GCSE, delivered online. Tutors are matched to the syllabus code, for example Cambridge 0580 Mathematics or 0625 Physics, and to the tier your child sits. We can prepare students for the May-June or October-November series and help them choose between Core and Extended if the school has not yet decided." },
    { question: "Do tutors come to homes in Pattukkottai?", answer: "No, tutors do not visit homes in Pattukkottai. In-person home tuition is limited to Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. What we offer is online home tuition: a live one-to-one lesson that your child takes at home on a laptop, with the tutor sharing papers and a whiteboard on screen. Many families find this easier than travelling into Thanjavur for classes." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tutoring cost in Pattukkottai?", answer: "The rate depends on the level, the subject and how many lessons a week you book, and it is quoted to you in writing before you pay anything. IB HL subjects and less common IGCSE papers usually cost more than Core-level work because fewer tutors teach them. Nothing is added for your town, and stopping or pausing is free. A trial lesson is included." },
    { question: "Which schools in Pattukkottai offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "We could not confirm any school in Pattukkottai that teaches the IB or Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE, so we name none. The closest one we verified is Yagappa International School at Sengipatti in Thanjavur district, which teaches Cambridge IGCSE. Trichy, Madurai and Chennai have larger groups. Please confirm current programmes with a school before relying on this." },
    { question: "My child boards at an international school elsewhere. Can a tutor help during holidays?", answer: "Yes, and this is one of the most common reasons families contact us. A tutor can run a short intensive during a break at home in Pattukkottai, reviewing topics the school has covered and marking timed papers. Tell us the boarding school's board and exam dates, and we will plan the block so that feedback arrives while there is still time to use it." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before we commit?", answer: "Yes, every match starts with a free trial lesson on a topic your child is actually studying. You can see how the tutor explains, what questions they ask and how your child responds, without paying or signing anything. If the fit is wrong, we offer a different tutor. There is no obligation to continue after the trial." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments and the Extended Essay?", answer: "A tutor can explain the criteria, discuss how to choose a workable topic and give feedback on drafts your child has written, but will not write, edit or complete any assessed work. IAs, Extended Essays, TOK essays and coursework must be your child's own. That protects the student's grade and their integrity with the IB." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can tutors cover for Pattukkottai students?", answer: "Tutors cover Maths AA and AI, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, Computer Science, English A, Psychology, ESS, Geography, History, and languages such as Tamil and Hindi. If your subject is not listed, tell us, and we will check whether we have a suitable tutor. All are offered at Higher and Standard Level where the IB allows." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Pattukkottai?", answer: "Yes. MYP tutoring focuses on the criteria, command terms and the Personal Project, and PYP support focuses on reading, number sense and unit work. Most Pattukkottai enquiries at these levels come from returning families whose children started the programme abroad or at a boarding school, and who want continuity while they settle." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as sitting with a tutor?", answer: "For most students, yes, provided the connection and workspace are reliable. The tutor sees the same work, marks the same papers and explains on a shared whiteboard. Some younger children need shorter sessions and more interaction. We suggest a quiet corner, headphones and a backup data option, particularly in monsoon weeks when power and mobile data can be unpredictable." },
    { question: "How are tutors chosen and checked?", answer: "Each tutor is reviewed for subject knowledge, recent experience with the specific IB or IGCSE course and the ability to explain clearly. We look at the syllabus they have taught and how they approach marking, not only at qualifications. You can judge the final fit yourself in the free trial lesson, and change the tutor if it does not suit." },
    { question: "When should a Pattukkottai student start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally several months before an important milestone, such as a move to an international school, the Class 11 start or an exam series. Starting early lets a tutor close gaps calmly. If you are already close to an exam, a shorter focused block on the highest-mark topics can still help, though it is better to begin earlier where possible." },
    { question: "My child is moving from Tamil Nadu State Board to IGCSE. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes. A tutor compares the State Board syllabus with the IGCSE one, finds the gaps, and builds English-language subject vocabulary. The biggest adjustments are usually exam style, tier choice and the practical skills paper in sciences. Starting two or three months before the switch makes the first term far less stressful for the student." },
    { question: "Can classes run on weekends or evenings?", answer: "Yes, most Pattukkottai families choose weekday evenings or weekend mornings. We avoid school hours and plan around festival weeks, heavy rain alerts and power cuts where we can. If a lesson is lost to an outage, we reschedule it without penalty, and the tutor can share notes so that little time is wasted." },
    { question: "What if we are unhappy with the tutor?", answer: "Tell us, and we will find a different tutor, usually within days and without charging for the change. A poor fit is not your child's fault or yours. There is no long contract, so you are never locked in, and the lesson notes carry over so the new tutor can continue from where the last one stopped." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school or exam board?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to the IB, Cambridge, Pearson Edexcel or any school named on this page. School names are given for context only and may change. We cannot arrange admissions, and we do not claim that a tutor will secure a particular grade or university place." },
  ],

